+# Private PID namespace and strict native observation
+
+One authorized fresh GPT-6 Luna/low utility `/root/pid_namespace_native_proof`
+completed the related batch on2026-10-04, exact clean provider
+`de874bc39553f8955cecdfaaeb4216959b40bd3c`. Command:
+`bash /tmp/automatic-session-slugs-pid-boundary-native-run.sh`.
+Result: failed, exit1,23s wall. No retry, cancellation or remaining operation.
+
+Source was quick-checked and independently reviewed before this execution.
+The native ELF and original catalog/source are unchanged from the prior pinned
+0.160 run; hashes remain those recorded in static-profile-native-observation.md.
+The batch runs the non-model ownership selector first and proceeds only after
+its success. Both use owning cached Nix with GOWORK=off/TMPDIR=/tmp and
+-mod=readonly; original180s fixture/10s utility/2s stop bounds are preserved.
+No production serving instance, auth home, package activation or live POST.
+
+## Positive ownership control
+
+`TestEphemeralNamespaceOwnershipIntegration` passed. Both actual cycles report
+exactly2 direct waits,2 adopted descendant reaps, ECHILD and surviving namespace
+init. This exercises real setsid and orphan adoption within the proven private
+reexec/proc boundary, and the second start/stop succeeds after the first domain
+is positively empty. Outer control0.14s; inner0.12s. This is actual kernel/process
+boundary evidence, not a complete native model/persistence pass.
+
+## Strict native result and limits
+
+`TestEphemeralProtocolIntegration` then ran and failed at its original strict
+logging gate. All38 phase records have fixed deny2->2/no unavailable sample.
+No tool-schema mismatch metadata was emitted. Dynamic-catalog refusal and CLI
+startup precedence controls passed; baseline reaches actual HTTP fallback POSTs.
+Existing actual-ID question/lost-reply/hostile-dispatch cases still execute with
+the existing assertions. HTTP/SSE observations do not prove successful WS frames.
+
+No changed snapshot/memory baseline, failed seed equality, denied-egress change
+or retained-root continuity error was reported. Unlike the prior run, comparisons
+reached the logger scan without those earlier mismatch failures. This does not
+retroactively attribute the old writer or establish all later persistence gates.
+
+28 bounded SQLite diagnostics report `logs_2.sqlite`, table `logs`, both utility
+prompt and owned thread/turn identity, UnknownOwner=false. All are truncated at
+the64-statement bound; no row/prompt/identity bytes are copied here. The matching
+error is "utility prompt persisted in SQLite". The test remains failed; no
+logger exception or all-store/isolation acceptance follows. Fresh MCP,
+managed-conflict and later final gates remain uncompleted because the strict
+failure stops progress before them.
+
+Raw log/status/elapsed: `/tmp/automatic-session-slugs-pid-native.{log,exit,elapsed}`.
+Safe parsed phase/tool/SQLite metadata:
+`/tmp/automatic-session-slugs-pid-native-summary.json`. These are private local
+artifacts; this document preserves bounded classifications and counts only.
+
+## Next decision
+
+Required logging preference is still unanswered: accept existing native
+logging with model naming; use deterministic naming without a model call; or
+expand scope to Codex logging suppression. No preselection/time or the earlier
+model/tools choice supplies that consent. No unchanged-source rerun or privacy
+waiver is selected. After a decision, reconcile the supported logging boundary
+in design/source/docs and related review, then complete exact consumer pins,
+new package/resources/CI, managed-child VM, final history review, deployment and
+real MODEL/custom/replay retained canaries. Earlier package evidence is qualified
+at its own revisions. Session remains active/unmerged; no merge direction.
